---
import results from "../../../public/data/historical-comparison/results.json";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const names: Record<string, string> = {
	"google:gemini-3.7-flash": "Gemini 3.7 Flash",
	"openai:gpt-5.6-luna": "GPT-5.6 Luna",
};
---
<Layout title="Historical full-packet results | LegalForecastBench" description="Separate exploratory results reconstructed from two saved runs on the earlier 100-case corpus, with prediction failures and outcome coverage disclosed.">
  <section class="prose-lfb prose mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
    <a href="/data/run-notes/">← Run notes</a>
    <h1>Historical full-packet results</h1>
    <p>These two saved runs used the earlier 100-case corpus, before the corpus factory cutover. They are exploratory historical results: the earlier corpus had missing filed oppositions, and these results are separate from the current 91-case comparison and its rankings.</p>
    <p>Both configurations requested high reasoning with the older Inspect AI full-packet backend. Each case recorded one model request and no tool calls. These records do not establish execution with the current native document-tool agent. GPT-5.6 Luna requested the Flex service tier.</p>
    <p>The original cohort contains 425 prediction units. Frozen labels provide binary outcomes for 385 units; 40 have null outcomes and are excluded from scoring. Six cases have no scored outcomes. We retain the original units and null labels in the reproduction download.</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>Accepted / attempted cases</th><th>Scored cases / units</th><th>Micro Brier</th><th>Equal-case Brier</th><th>All-execution estimated cost</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{results.conditions.map(row => <tr><td>{names[row.model_id]}</td><td>{row.accepted_cases} / {row.attempted_cases}</td><td>{row.scored_cases} / {row.scored_units}</td><td>{row.micro_brier.toFixed(6)}</td><td>{row.equal_case_brier.toFixed(6)}</td><td>${row.estimated_all_execution_cost_usd.toFixed(6)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>GPT-5.6 Luna omitted a required unit in each of two cases (71396055 and 71648352). We exclude both entire case outputs, dropping 18 labelled units, rather than inventing probabilities. Its scores cover 367 units from 92 cases with outcomes, compared with Gemini’s 385 units from 94 cases. These unequal denominators do not support a ranking or significance claim.</p>
    <p>Recorded token usage and estimated costs cover all 100 executions per configuration and agree with their saved accounting records. Luna’s accepted 98-case workload estimate is $3.571631; its all-execution estimate includes the two rejected cases. These are recorded estimates, not provider invoices or standard-rate repricing. Cache dimensions and billing evidence are unavailable here.</p>
    <h2>Reproduce without model calls</h2>
    <p><a href="/data/historical-comparison/inputs.json" download>Download original unit probabilities, nullable outcomes, usage, and run identities</a> · <a href="/data/historical-comparison/results.json" download>Download reconstructed results and failed-case details</a></p>
    <p>From the repository checkout, run:</p>
    <pre><code>uv run python scripts/reproduce_historical_comparison.py site/public/data/historical-comparison/inputs.json /tmp/historical-results.json</code></pre>
    <p>The script validates case and unit coverage, rejects malformed or defaulted inputs, and uses the benchmark’s shared scorer for micro and equal-case Brier. The sanitized extract contains no court documents, model rationales, or private operating records. Saved run IDs are {results.conditions.map(row => row.run_id).join(" and ")}.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
